<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Maritime Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Tallo Kingdom</h1><p class="st-meta">1450 CE – 1906 CE (approx.) · capital Tallo</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Makassar kingdom joined with Gowa in a twin state, whose rulers served as chancellors and led South Sulawesi's conversion to Islam.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Tallo was founded in the 15th century, according to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/gowa-sultanate">Makassar</a> chronicles, by a prince of Gowa who left after a succession dispute and settled near the mouth of the Tallo River, north of today's Makassar city. In the early 16th century the two kingdoms swore an alliance and came to act as one state, described in the saying 'one people, two kings'.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The ruler of Tallo usually served as chancellor of Gowa. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karaeng-matoaya">Karaeng Matoaya</a> was the first <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/gowa-sultanate">Makassar</a> ruler to accept <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a>, in 1605, and guided the expansion of the joint state. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karaeng-pattingalloang">Karaeng Pattingalloang</a>, famous for his learning, collected European books, maps and a globe.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Tallo shared the fate of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/gowa-sultanate">Gowa Sultanate</a>, losing power after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-bongaya">Treaty of Bongaya</a> of 1667 and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> conquest of South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sulawesi">Sulawesi</a> in 1906. Its name survives in a district of Makassar, where the royal tombs of Tallo still stand.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/tallo-kingdom.jpg" alt="Tallo Kingdom" width="320" height="427"><figcaption>Image: Cahyo Ramadhani · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gravestone_in_kings_of_Tallo_burial_site.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1450 CE – 1906 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Tallo</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Karaeng Matoaya</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Makassarese</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Indonesia</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Tallo</dd></dl></aside></div>

